{
 "_createdAt": "2026-04-27T19:17:42Z",
 "_id": "wp-post-134733-en",
 "_rev": "S0nWQbQfCu6sjLYYx5pLN3",
 "_type": "article",
 "_updatedAt": "2026-11-09T18:01:04Z",
 "author": {
  "_ref": "author-legacy-archive",
  "_type": "reference"
 },
 "body": [
  {
   "_key": "000000000001",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000000",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "April is a very usable month for Egypt travel."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000003",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "57n8kyx3b4n3",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Not crammed like the winter peak, not yet ruled by summer heat. "
    },
    {
     "_key": "nfwyb2d8fkgn",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "v84l49g3jxhx"
     ],
     "text": "Cairo"
    },
    {
     "_key": "mfu6ao39g70t",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": " and "
    },
    {
     "_key": "ohu0ldoho8f0",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "z9d1rsuqflm4"
     ],
     "text": "Giza"
    },
    {
     "_key": "2bigpl4tosdb",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": ", "
    },
    {
     "_key": "9vkvbsw20b4l",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "pb1hhoig9laq"
     ],
     "text": "Luxor"
    },
    {
     "_key": "n7ivjm1qzdm3",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": ", "
    },
    {
     "_key": "85ykikapsysl",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "yw5cyc7q1ef6"
     ],
     "text": "Aswan"
    },
    {
     "_key": "19xerdez13aq",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": ", and the Red Sea all fit one itinerary; morning sightseeing and afternoon rest combine easily."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [
    {
     "_key": "v84l49g3jxhx",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "wp-page-83284",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    },
    {
     "_key": "z9d1rsuqflm4",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "wp-page-58854",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    },
    {
     "_key": "pb1hhoig9laq",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "wp-page-58877",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    },
    {
     "_key": "yw5cyc7q1ef6",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "wp-page-58758",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    }
   ],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000005",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000004",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "But April isn't entirely calm."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000007",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000006",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "In Upper Egypt, days can grow quite hot. The springtime khamaseen — dust-laden wind — can blow. Sham El-Nessim, Coptic Easter, and in some years Ramadan or Eid timing can overlap, affecting domestic travel and hotel crowding."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000009",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000008",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "April Egypt is a good season. Using it well takes a little strategy."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000000b",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000000a",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "What April Egypt is like"
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "h2"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000000d",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000000c",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "April sits at the boundary from winter into summer."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000000f",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "v82nrmda6z0n",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "In Cairo and Giza, days are warm, mornings and nights relatively passable. Pyramids, Saqqara, Islamic Cairo, "
    },
    {
     "_key": "x2tgsaiquiyj",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "dwtyodg2s1ua"
     ],
     "text": "Coptic Cairo"
    },
    {
     "_key": "luft1cs5zb74",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": ", and the Grand Egyptian Museum combine — a very mobile period."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [
    {
     "_key": "dwtyodg2s1ua",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "wp-page-63606",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    }
   ],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000011",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000010",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "In Luxor and Aswan, daytime heat starts strengthening. Especially in the latter half, long afternoon outdoor walks tire. Still, early morning into late morning gives excellent site-touring conditions. Without summer's harshness, with winter's crowds slightly easing."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000013",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000012",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "The Red Sea coast is quite appealing in April. Good for seaside rest, diving, and snorkelling. Easier to enter water than winter, not yet midsummer hot — a usable month for combining sea and sites."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000015",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000014",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Desert and oases are doable but need care. White Desert and Siwa are beautiful, but spring wind, daytime heat, and long-distance transfer call for margin-built itineraries."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000017",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000016",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Why April fits"
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "h2"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000019",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000018",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "April's strength is option breadth."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000001b",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "a2gsoxdo44yk",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "See museum and pyramids in Cairo. Walk "
    },
    {
     "_key": "aj6z6i2lie72",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "fukc0pqpayom"
     ],
     "text": "Valley of the Kings"
    },
    {
     "_key": "ozbwiyesxze8",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": " and temples in Luxor. Rest along the Nile in Aswan. Spend several days on the Red Sea. These combinations work relatively without strain."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [
    {
     "_key": "fukc0pqpayom",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "guideArticle.luxor.valley-of-the-kings",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    }
   ],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000001d",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000001c",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Midsummer makes Luxor and Aswan outdoor touring quite harsh. Winter is comfortable but popular, with hotel and cruise competition strong. April sits between."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000001f",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000001e",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Using morning time well shows main sites in good conditions. Don't pack afternoon — leave hotel, Nile-side, museum, car transfer, and short rest. April matches this rhythm."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000021",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000020",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "This month suits travel that deeply combines preferred regions while avoiding heat, rather than \"all of Egypt a little.\""
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000023",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000022",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Working with heat"
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "h2"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000025",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000024",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "What matters most in April Egypt is timing."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000027",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000026",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "In Cairo and Giza, early morning into late morning walks easily, afternoon still works. But at exposed places like pyramids or Saqqara, sun-blocking is scarce — hat and water needed."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000029",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "moqhsvwn0lu0",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "In Luxor, early morning west bank is basic. Valley of the Kings, Hatshepsut, "
    },
    {
     "_key": "gyhim4y9rzpt",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "ace708raj9vi"
     ],
     "text": "Medinet Habu"
    },
    {
     "_key": "mc49zbox6eub",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": ", nobles' tombs — see in morning for comfort. Pushing around midday weakens impressions in heat."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [
    {
     "_key": "ace708raj9vi",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "guideArticle.luxor.madinat-habu-temple",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    }
   ],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000002b",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "xnl81kt19qan",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "In Aswan, morning Philae or Unfinished Obelisk, afternoon Nile-side rest fits. For "
    },
    {
     "_key": "9s16qgphw8n1",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "c58pu4y1z4gu"
     ],
     "text": "Abu Simbel"
    },
    {
     "_key": "ixjhm3xb70o9",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": " days, early-morning departure is common; use the whole day for transfer and touring."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [
    {
     "_key": "c58pu4y1z4gu",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "wp-page-56813",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    }
   ],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000002d",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000002c",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "April isn't yet a \"too hot to travel\" month. But it isn't \"walk outside all day\" either. Use morning, slack midday — that makes April trips good."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000002f",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000002e",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Watch for khamaseen"
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "h2"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000031",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000030",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "In spring Egypt, the khamaseen — hot dry wind — can blow."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000033",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000032",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Wind carrying sand and dust, lowering visibility, making air feel heavy, sometimes spiking temperature. People with weak respiration, with children, elderly, and those planning desert tours need caution."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000035",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000034",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Khamaseen days make open-site or desert sightseeing hard. Build itinerary margin — indoor museums, hotel rest, short transfer days — that you can swap in."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000037",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000036",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "This isn't reason to avoid April. It's just reality to know when travelling spring Egypt."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000039",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000038",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "April Cairo and Giza"
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "h2"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000003b",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000003a",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "April Cairo combines city-walking and museum easily."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000003d",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000003c",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "For Giza pyramids, try morning. Before sun strengthens walks easier, with softer photo light. For Great Sphinx, panorama point, and pyramid-surround movement, secure morning time."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000003f",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000003e",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "The Grand Egyptian Museum fits Giza-area itinerary. The official ticket site notes a visit includes the Tutankhamun Galleries, Main Galleries, Grand Hall, Grand Staircase, and Khufu Boat Museum. Quantity is large — taking substantial time satisfies more than rushing."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000041",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000040",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "The Egyptian Museum at Tahrir Square holds old-museum atmosphere and collection depth. But for Tutankhamun main display, the centre is the Grand Egyptian Museum. Organise by purpose."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000043",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "58o2blf30pnp",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Islamic Cairo and "
    },
    {
     "_key": "yr68rzwexlps",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "ayjqhqw7pta7"
     ],
     "text": "Khan el-Khalili"
    },
    {
     "_key": "aacxngliz1gl",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": " walk well morning or evening. Around al-Muizz Street, architectural density is high — walking in April's not-too-hot hours leaves impression."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [
    {
     "_key": "ayjqhqw7pta7",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "guideArticle.cairo.khan-el-khalili",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    }
   ],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000045",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000044",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "April Luxor"
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "h2"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000047",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000046",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "April Luxor is about morning."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000049",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "iu2sa4x6oz94",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Valley of the Kings, "
    },
    {
     "_key": "lkkbrwjex6as",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "wbh1v101wqtg"
     ],
     "text": "Valley of the Queens"
    },
    {
     "_key": "xv4gxtky3i68",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": ", nobles' tombs, "
    },
    {
     "_key": "tfpx35wb7ufk",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "8rghtteakp4e"
     ],
     "text": "Deir el-Medina"
    },
    {
     "_key": "ur7nnc8xy7fu",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": ", Hatshepsut, and Medinet Habu all involve outdoor movement. Leaving early lets you see a lot before heat strengthens."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [
    {
     "_key": "wbh1v101wqtg",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "guideArticle.luxor.valley-of-the-queens",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    },
    {
     "_key": "8rghtteakp4e",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "guideArticle.luxor.deir-el-madina",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    }
   ],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000004b",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "eiwvfultwh92",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "East bank — how to split Karnak and "
    },
    {
     "_key": "ghrr1h598cm0",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "8zumd428xzao"
     ],
     "text": "Luxor Temple"
    },
    {
     "_key": "3dlp3w8h37vv",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": " matters. Karnak is wide; morning gives viewing margin. Luxor Temple comes alive evening into night — place later both for atmosphere and heat-avoidance."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [
    {
     "_key": "8zumd428xzao",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "guideArticle.luxor.the-luxor-temple",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    }
   ],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000004d",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000004c",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "In April Luxor, build midday rest into the itinerary. Return to hotel, lunch Nile-side, pool or shade rest. This isn't laziness — it's judgment protecting afternoon and next-day touring quality."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000004f",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000004e",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "For first Luxor, minimum two nights, ideally three. April needs moving while avoiding daytime heat — too-short stays pack sites."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000051",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000050",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "April Aswan"
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "h2"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000053",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000052",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Aswan is warm in April and can feel hot daytime."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000055",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000054",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Even so, Nile scenery, Philae, felucca, Nubian culture, and island scenery match this season. Placing slightly slower than Luxor at trip's back half balances well."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000057",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000056",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Philae is beautiful on water — morning visit is comfortable. Combining Unfinished Obelisk or High Dam, move before sun strengthens."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000059",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000058",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "For Abu Simbel in April, heat-protection still needed. Often early-morning departure with long transfer — give before-and-after days margin. Cutting Aswan to one night to fit Abu Simbel rushes things."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000005b",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000005a",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Nile cruise and April"
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "h2"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000005d",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000005c",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "April suits Nile cruises too."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000005f",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "dfpo3krrpt4v",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Cooler than winter peak; deck time stays enjoyable without summer heat. Moving between Luxor and Aswan, fitting in "
    },
    {
     "_key": "mdf5lkbt2zdh",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "bp7e6bjjuysf"
     ],
     "text": "Edfu"
    },
    {
     "_key": "mkcr7f4oc6qk",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": ", "
    },
    {
     "_key": "qidsbsueg6t6",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "reltkgf4qszk"
     ],
     "text": "Kom Ombo"
    },
    {
     "_key": "e219nwv9h41v",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": ", and Philae — large benefit for first Egypt travellers."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [
    {
     "_key": "bp7e6bjjuysf",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "wp-page-58841",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    },
    {
     "_key": "reltkgf4qszk",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "wp-page-58875",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    }
   ],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000061",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000060",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Even on cruise, push tour time to morning. Edfu and Kom Ombo temples have sun-hard places — confirm ship schedule and tour time."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000063",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000062",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Choosing a ship, confirm cabin, meals, guide, fees, tips, and optional-tour handling beyond price. April isn't full off-season, so good ships and small ships need earlier booking."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000065",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000064",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Combining Red Sea"
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "h2"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000067",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000066",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "April Red Sea is a strong choice."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000069",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000068",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Hurghada, El Gouna, Marsa Alam, Sharm el-Sheikh, Dahab — usable for seaside rest, diving, and snorkelling. Easier to enter water than winter, summer heat not yet full."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000006b",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000006a",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Moving from Luxor to Hurghada for several rest days is realistic for sites-plus-sea. Sharm el-Sheikh and Dahab need separate transfer but appeal to those seeking Sinai's sea-and-mountain feel."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000006d",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000006c",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Including Red Sea, placing at the end eases the body. After Cairo, Luxor, and Aswan sites, several seaside rest days. In April this composition is very natural."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000006f",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000006e",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Sham El-Nessim and Coptic Easter"
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "h2"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000071",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000070",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "In April Egypt, Sham El-Nessim matters."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000073",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000072",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Sham El-Nessim is the spring holiday celebrated the day after Coptic Easter. Beyond religion, it's widely embraced — families head to parks, Nile-side, or seaside, bringing food for a day out."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000075",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000074",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Dates change yearly. Check your travel year's calendar."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000077",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000076",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Around this holiday, domestic travel rises. Around Ain Sokhna, Red Sea resorts, Alexandria, Nile-side parks, and popular hotels crowd. You feel the holiday atmosphere; movement and lodging need margin."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000079",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000078",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Around Coptic Easter, special services and people-flow appear at Coptic Cairo and major churches. Visiting, treat as religious occasion — quiet respect over tourist facility."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000007b",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000007a",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "When Ramadan or Eid overlaps"
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "h2"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000007d",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000007c",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Ramadan, based on the lunar calendar, moves about 11 days earlier yearly. Some years it overlaps April."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000007f",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000007e",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "During Ramadan, daytime food, opening hours, transport, and people-flow can shift from usual. At the same time, post-sunset iftar, city lights, and family-and-friend gatherings give a chance to feel Egyptian life deeply."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000081",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000080",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Around Eid al-Fitr, domestic travel and family movement rise. Hotels, trains, domestic flights, and tourist sites crowd — book early."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000083",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000082",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "For April travel, confirm early in planning where Ramadan, Eid, Coptic Easter, and Sham El-Nessim fall that year."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000085",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000084",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Dress and gear"
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "h2"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000087",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000086",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "April needs dress handling both sun and morning-night difference, not only summer wear."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000089",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000088",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "In Cairo and Giza, thin long sleeve, walkable pants, and light cover useful. In Luxor and Aswan, breathable clothes, hat, sunglasses, and sunscreen matter."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000008b",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000008a",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "At religious sites or conservative areas, shoulder/knee-covering dress reassures. A thin stole or long-sleeve shirt also blocks sun."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000008d",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000008c",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Choose footwear suited to site walking. Sand, stone steps, unpaved road, ship boarding — sandals alone tire."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000008f",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000008e",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Hydration matters. April runs dry for the temperature; without much sweat sensation, dehydration is easy."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000091",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000090",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Who April suits"
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "h2"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000093",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000092",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "April suits travellers wanting wide Egypt."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000095",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000094",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Combining Cairo and Giza, Luxor, Aswan, and Red Sea. Avoiding winter crowds slightly. Not heat-strong but wanting warm season travel. Combining site touring and seaside rest in one trip — a very good month."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000097",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000096",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Those highly heat-averse may find January or February better. Desert-centred trips fit winter more stably. Cheapest-seeking gets summer options, with heat cost."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000099",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000098",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "April isn't universal."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000009b",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000009a",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "But for combining many Egyptian appeals in one trip, a very balanced month."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000009d",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000009c",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Itinerary thinking"
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "h2"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000009f",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000009e",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "For first Egypt with 7 to 10 days, axis on Cairo and Giza, Luxor, and Aswan is natural. Adding Red Sea, place two or three nights at the end for body ease."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "0000000000a1",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "0000000000a0",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Short trip — narrow to Cairo and Luxor realistically. Giza pyramids, Grand Egyptian Museum, Valley of the Kings, and Karnak show the large ancient-Egyptian axis."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "0000000000a3",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "0000000000a2",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "For Nile cruise, minimum three nights, ideally four or more. Too short packs transfer and touring, losing river time."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "0000000000a5",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "0000000000a4",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "For desert or Siwa, secure separate days. April is doable, but transfer distance and weather call for margin rather than forced add."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "0000000000a7",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "0000000000a6",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Tips for a good April Egypt"
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "h2"
  },
  {
   "_key": "0000000000a9",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "0000000000a8",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Wake early."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "0000000000ab",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "0000000000aa",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Don't pack midday."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "0000000000ad",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "0000000000ac",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Confirm religious calendar and holidays."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "0000000000af",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "0000000000ae",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Hold flexible plans for khamaseen days."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "0000000000b1",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "0000000000b0",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Build in rest places like Red Sea or Aswan."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "0000000000b3",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "0000000000b2",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "These alone make April Egypt much easier."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "0000000000b5",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "0000000000b4",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "The month's appeal isn't deep winter coolness or summer's strong cheapness. It's warmth, light, mobility, slightly calmer crowds, and sea-and-site combinability. The balance."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "0000000000b7",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "0000000000b6",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "April Egypt rewards travellers who start the day a bit earlier."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "0000000000b9",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "0000000000b8",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Morning pyramids."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "0000000000bb",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "0000000000ba",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Late-morning Valley of the Kings."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "0000000000bd",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "0000000000bc",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Evening Nile."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "0000000000bf",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "0000000000be",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Several days later, Red Sea."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "0000000000c1",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "0000000000c0",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Building that flow, April shows Egypt very beautifully."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  }
 ],
